FORMAT: 1A
HOST: https://treento.onrender.com/

# Treento API

REST API for urban green space management: tree/green space consultation, reporting, and adoption.
Authentication via JWT (Bearer Token).

Protected endpoints require Authorization: Bearer <JWT_TOKEN>.
Admin endpoints require a valid token for an admin account.

## Authentication [/auth]

### Sign up [POST /auth/signup]
Creates a new user account.

+ Request (application/json)
    + Body
        {
            "email": "user1@test.com",
            "password": "Password123"
        }

+ Response 201
    + Body
        {
            "message": "User created successfully"
        }

+ Response 400 (application/json)
    + Body
        {
            "message": "Email and password are required"
        }

+ Response 400 (application/json)
    + Body
        {
            "message": "Invalid email format"
        }

+ Response 409 (application/json)
    + Body
        {
            "message": "User already exists"
        }

### Login [POST /auth/login]
Authenticates a user and returns a JWT token.

+ Request (application/json)
    + Body
        {
            "email": "user1@test.com",
            "password": "Password123"
        }

+ Response 200
    + Body
        {
            "token": "<JWT_TOKEN>"
        }

+ Response 400 (application/json)
    + Body
        {
            "message": "Email and password are required"
        }

+ Response 401 (application/json)
    + Body
        {
            "message": "Invalid email or password"
        }

### Get current user (debug) [GET /auth/me]
Returns the decoded JWT payload (debug endpoint). Authentication required.

+ Request
    + Headers
        Authorization: Bearer <JWT_TOKEN>

+ Response 200 (application/json)
    + Body
        {
            "user": {
                "userId": "<USER_ID>",
                "isAdmin": false
            }
        }

+ Response 401 (application/json)
    + Body
        {
            "message": "Unauthorized"
        }

## Trees [/trees]

### Get all trees [GET /trees]
Returns the list of trees available in the system.

+ Parameters
    + limit (optional, number) - Limits the number of returned trees

+ Response 200 (application/json)
    + Body
        [
            {
                "_id": "697b411cc780dee858429cc6",
                "species": "Tiglio selvatico",
                "scientificName": "Tilia cordata Mill.",
                "lat": 46.07970277777778,
                "lng": 11.543433333333333,
                "__v": 0
            },
            {
                "_id": "697b411cc780dee858429ccf",
                "species": "Larice",
                "scientificName": "Larix decidua Mill.",
                "lat": 46.491391666666665,
                "lng": 11.76961388888889,
                "__v": 0
            },
            {
                "_id": "697b411cc780dee858429cd4",
                "species": "Pino silvestre",
                "scientificName": "Insieme omogeneo di Pinus sylvestris L.",
                "lat": 46.28402777777777,
                "lng": 11.396266666666666,
                "__v": 0
            }
        ]

+ Response 400 (application/json)
    + Body
        {
            "message": "Invalid query parameter"
        }

+ Response 500 (application/json)
    + Body
        {
            "message": "Server error"
        }

### Get tree detail [GET /trees/{id}]
Returns the details of a specific tree by id.

+ Parameters
    + id (required, string) - Tree id (MongoDB ObjectId)

+ Response 200 (application/json)
    + Body
        {
            "_id": "697b411cc780dee858429cc6",
            "species": "Tiglio selvatico",
            "scientificName": "Tilia cordata Mill.",
            "lat": 46.07970277777778,
            "lng": 11.543433333333333,
            "__v": 0
        }

+ Response 400 (application/json)
    + Body
        {
            "message": "Invalid tree ID"
        }

+ Response 404 (application/json)
    + Body
        {
            "message": "Tree not found"
        }
        
## Reports [/reports]

### Create report [POST /reports]
Creates a new report. Authentication required.

+ Request (application/json)
    + Headers
        Authorization: Bearer <JWT_TOKEN>
    + Body
        {
            "title": "Broken tree",
            "location": "Via Roma"
        }

+ Response 201 (application/json)
    + Body
        {
            "message": "Report created successfully"
        }

+ Response 400 (application/json)
    + Body
        {
            "message": "Missing required fields"
        }

+ Response 401 (application/json)
    + Body
        {
            "message": "Unauthorized"
        }

+ Response 500 (application/json)
    + Body
        {
            "message": "Server error"
        }

### View my reports [GET /reports/me]
Returns reports created by the authenticated user.

+ Request
    + Headers
        Authorization: Bearer <JWT_TOKEN>

+ Response 200 (application/json)
    + Body
        [
            {
                "_id": "6965530792bc2e03a0590393",
                "title": "Broken tree",
                "location": "Via Roma",
                "userId": "69458745fc5b470c019c2320",
                "status": "IN_PROGRESS",
                "createdAt": "2026-01-12T20:01:11.602Z",
                "updatedAt": "2026-01-12T20:40:52.068Z",
                "__v": 0
            },
            {
                "_id": "695d339a1cd8874b5ba2356f",
                "title": "Broken tree",
                "location": "Via Roma",
                "userId": "69458745fc5b470c019c2320",
                "status": "OPEN",
                "createdAt": "2026-01-06T16:08:58.734Z",
                "updatedAt": "2026-01-06T16:08:58.734Z",
                "__v": 0
            }
        ]

+ Response 401 (application/json)
    + Body
        {
            "message": "Unauthorized"
        }

+ Response 500 (application/json)
    + Body
        {
            "message": "Server error"
        }

### Admin list reports [GET /reports]
Returns all reports (admin only).

+ Request
    + Headers
        Authorization: Bearer <ADMIN_JWT_TOKEN>

+ Response 200 (application/json)
    + Body
        [
            {
                "_id": "6965530792bc2e03a0590393",
                "title": "Broken tree",
                "location": "Via Roma",
                "userId": "69458745fc5b470c019c2320",
                "status": "IN_PROGRESS",
                "createdAt": "2026-01-12T20:01:11.602Z",
                "updatedAt": "2026-01-12T20:40:52.068Z",
                "__v": 0
            },
            {
                "_id": "695d339a1cd8874b5ba2356f",
                "title": "Broken tree",
                "location": "Via Roma",
                "userId": "69458745fc5b470c019c2320",
                "status": "OPEN",
                "createdAt": "2026-01-06T16:08:58.734Z",
                "updatedAt": "2026-01-06T16:08:58.734Z",
                "__v": 0
            }
        ]

+ Response 401 (application/json)
    + Body
        {
            "message": "Unauthorized"
        }

+ Response 403 (application/json)
    + Body
        {
            "message": "Forbidden"
        }
        
+ Response 500 (application/json)
    + Body
        {
            "message": "Server error"
        }        

### Admin update report status [PATCH /reports/{id}/status]
Updates the status of a report (admin only).

Allowed statuses: `OPEN`, `IN_PROGRESS`, `CLOSED`.

+ Parameters
    + id (required, string) - Report id (MongoDB ObjectId)

+ Request (application/json)
    + Headers
        Authorization: Bearer <ADMIN_JWT_TOKEN>
    + Body
        {
            "status": "IN_PROGRESS"
        }

+ Response 200 (application/json)
    + Body
        {
            "_id": "695d339a1cd8874b5ba2356f",
            "title": "Broken tree",
            "location": "Via Roma",
            "userId": "69458745fc5b470c019c2320",
            "status": "IN_PROGRESS",
            "createdAt": "2026-01-06T16:08:58.734Z",
            "updatedAt": "2026-01-06T16:10:20.112Z",
            "__v": 0
        }

+ Response 400 (application/json)
    + Body
        {
            "message": "Invalid report id"
        }

+ Response 400 (application/json)
    + Body
        {
            "message": "Invalid status"
        }

+ Response 401 (application/json)
    + Body
        {
            "message": "Unauthorized"
        }

+ Response 403 (application/json)
    + Body
        {
            "message": "Forbidden"
        }

+ Response 404 (application/json)
    + Body
        {
            "message": "Report not found"
        }

+ Response 500 (application/json)
    + Body
        {
            "message": "Server error"
        }
        
## Adoptions [/adoptions]

### Create adoption request [POST /adoptions]
Creates an adoption request for a tree. Authentication required.

+ Request (application/json)
    + Headers
        Authorization: Bearer <JWT_TOKEN>
    + Body
        {
          "treeId": "697b411cc780dee858429cc6"
        }

+ Response 201 (application/json)
    + Body
        {
          "message": "Adoption request created successfully"
        }

+ Response 400 (application/json)
    + Body
        {
          "message": "Missing required fields"
        }

+ Response 400 (application/json)
    + Body
        {
          "message": "Invalid tree ID"
        }

+ Response 401 (application/json)
    + Body
        {
          "message": "Unauthorized"
        }

### Get all adoption requests (admin) [GET /adoptions]
Returns all adoption requests (admin only).

+ Request
    + Headers
        Authorization: Bearer <ADMIN_JWT_TOKEN>

+ Response 200 (application/json)
    + Body
        [
            {
                "_id": "69676977641746e3c953d24c",
                "treeId": {
                        "_id": "697b411cc780dee858429cc6",
                        "species": "Tiglio selvatico",
                        "scientificName": "Tilia cordata Mill.",
                        "lat": 46.07970277777778,
                        "lng": 11.543433333333333,
                        "__v": 0
                },
                "userId": {
                    "_id": "...",
                    "email": "user1@test.com"
                },
                "status": "APPROVED",
                "createdAt": "2026-01-14T10:01:27.883Z",
                "updatedAt": "2026-01-14T10:57:11.615Z",
                "__v": 0
            },
            {
                "_id": "6967935b211dca582027194a",
                "treeId": {
                    "_id": "697b411cc780dee858429cc6",
                    "species": "Tiglio selvatico",
                    "scientificName": "Tilia cordata Mill.",
                    "lat": 46.07970277777778,
                    "lng": 11.543433333333333,
                    "__v": 0
                },
                "userId": {
                    "_id": "...",
                    "email": "user1@test.com"
                },
                "status": "PENDING",
                "createdAt": "2026-01-14T13:00:11.656Z",
                "updatedAt": "2026-01-14T13:00:11.656Z",
                "__v": 0
            }
        ]

+ Response 401 (application/json)
    + Body
        {
          "message": "Unauthorized"
        }

+ Response 403 (application/json)
    + Body
        {
          "message": "Forbidden"
        }
        

### Get my adoption requests [GET /adoptions/me]
Returns adoption requests created by the authenticated user.

+ Request
    + Headers
        Authorization: Bearer <JWT_TOKEN>

+ Response 200 (application/json)
    + Body
        [
          {
            "_id": "69676977641746e3c953d24c",
            "treeId": {
                        "_id": "697b411cc780dee858429cc6",
                        "species": "Tiglio selvatico",
                        "scientificName": "Tilia cordata Mill.",
                        "lat": 46.07970277777778,
                        "lng": 11.543433333333333,
                        "__v": 0
                },
                "userId": "69458745fc5b470c019c2320",
                "status": "APPROVED",
                "createdAt": "2026-01-14T10:01:27.883Z",
                "updatedAt": "2026-01-14T10:57:11.615Z",
                "__v": 0
            }
        ]

+ Response 401 (application/json)
    + Body
        {
          "message": "Unauthorized"
        }


### Update adoption status (admin) [PATCH /adoptions/{id}/status]
Updates adoption request status (admin only).

Allowed status values: `PENDING`, `APPROVED`, `REJECTED`.

+ Parameters
    + id (required, string) - Adoption id

+ Request (application/json)
    + Headers
        Authorization: Bearer <ADMIN_JWT_TOKEN>
    + Body
        {
          "status": "APPROVED"
        }

+ Response 200 (application/json)
    + Body
        {
            "_id": "69676977641746e3c953d24c",
            "treeId": "697b411cc780dee858429cc6",
            "userId": "69458745fc5b470c019c2320",
            "status": "APPROVED",
            "createdAt": "2026-01-14T10:01:27.883Z",
            "updatedAt": "2026-01-14T13:09:18.948Z",
            "__v": 0
        }

+ Response 400 (application/json)
    + Body
        {
          "message": "Invalid adoption id"
        }

+ Response 400 (application/json)
    + Body
        {
          "message": "Invalid status"
        }

+ Response 401 (application/json)
    + Body
        {
          "message": "Unauthorized"
        }

+ Response 403 (application/json)
    + Body
        {
          "message": "Forbidden"
        }

+ Response 404 (application/json)
    + Body
        {
          "message": "Adoption not found"
        }